     useful when driver knows that ddeessttrrooyy__ddeevv__sscchheedd() is called for all in‐
     stantiated devices, but need to postpone module unload until
     ddeessttrrooyy__ddeevv() is actually finished for all of them.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, mmaakkee__ddeevv__ss() and mmaakkee__ddeevv__pp() will return 0, otherwise
     they will return an error.  If successful, mmaakkee__ddeevv__ccrreeddff() will return a
     valid _c_d_e_v pointer, otherwise it will return NULL.

EERRRROORRSS
     The mmaakkee__ddeevv__ss(), mmaakkee__ddeevv__pp() and mmaakkee__ddeevv__aalliiaass__pp() calls will fail and
     the device will be not registered if:

     [ENOMEM]           The MAKEDEV_NOWAIT flag was specified and a memory al‐
                        location request could not be satisfied.

     [ENAMETOOLONG]     The MAKEDEV_CHECKNAME flag was specified and the pro‐
                        vided device name is longer than SPECNAMELEN.

     [EINVAL]           The MAKEDEV_CHECKNAME flag was specified and the pro‐
                        vided device name is empty, contains a "." or ".."
                        path component or ends with ‘/’.

     [EINVAL]           The MAKEDEV_CHECKNAME flag was specified and the pro‐
                        vided device name contains invalid characters.

     [EEXIST]           The MAKEDEV_CHECKNAME flag was specified and the pro‐
                        vided device name already exists.

